--TEST--
`Core\Ldap\Connection::add` refuses an attribute name that can come from outside the program, from a literal's key and from an array whose keys a visitor chose, and admits a `tainted` value under a written name — `rule:core-classes/ldap-filter-is-a-value`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:types/qualifiers-tainted-and-secret
// A program adds a directory entry from a form. The three attribute names a visitor chose are errors.
// The count of errors is the assertion.
var $corp = Core\Ldap::connect("corp-accounts");
string $person = "CN=Lena Vogt,OU=Bakery,DC=example,DC=test";
tainted string $field = Core\Request::post("field") ?? "title";
tainted string $value = Core\Request::post("value") ?? "Baker";
array<tainted string> $form = Core\Request::postArray("entry");

$corp->add($person, ["objectClass" => "user", $field => $value]);
$corp->add($person, $form);
$corp->add($person, ["objectClass" => "user", ...$form]);

// A `tainted` value under a name the program wrote is allowed.
string $name = "description";
$corp->add($person, ["objectClass" => "user", "title" => $value, $name => $value]);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: an LDAP attribute name can come from outside the program
%A
error[E0401]: an LDAP attribute name can come from outside the program
%A
error[E0401]: an LDAP attribute name can come from outside the program
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
